lose.shift(15) - 1 → 10d momentum skipping 5d\\n- mom_120d_skip5: presumably close.shift(5)/close.shift(125) - 1\\n- vix_beta_cond_60x20: conditional VIX beta\\n- vol_of_vol20x60: vol of vol\\n\\nFor new factors, I want low correlation with these. Ideas with strong differentiation:\\n- **Range position (close location value, CLV)**: very different from momentum\\n- **Skewness**: different\\n- **Amihud illiquidity**: different\\n- **DXY beta**: macro, different\\n- **Relative strength z-score**: could correlate with momentum\\n\\nLet me first build the framework and test a batch of candidate factors in one script (the skill says validate only ONE idea per script, but I can first run a screening script to explore, then do focused validation per candidate). Actually the skill says \"Validate only ONE idea (i.e. single type of factor) per script\". To be efficient, I\\'ll create a shared research module `scripts/factor_research_lib.py` that provides the panel loading and IC computation, then individual scripts for each candidate factor. But tool calls are expensive; a screening script that prints metrics for several candidate factor families is fine as \"exploration\", then focused validation scripts per candidate. Let me do a screening script first with a few factor families, then run focused scripts for the promising ones (to also produce the persistence-ready metrics).\\n\\nActually, given the constraint \"Validate only ONE idea per script\", I\\'ll interpret: one script per factor family. But for exploration, I can write a single exploration script that computes metrics for multiple candidates and prints them — that\\'s exploration, not final validation. Then for persistence, each factor gets its own script run to confirm. To be efficient, I\\'ll do:\\n\\n1. `scripts/miner_1_20260730_research_lib.py` — shared library (panel loading, IC computation)\\n2. `scripts/miner_1_20260730_explore_batch1.py` — explore ~8 candidate factor families, print metrics\\n3. Based on results, focused validation + persistence for winners\\n\\nLet me write the shared library first.\\n\\nKey design decisions for IC computation:\\n- Cross-section: 15 assets\\n- For each date t, factor value computed from data up to t (no lookahead)\\n- Forward return: `close[t+h]/close[t] - 1` where h is horizon in trading days\\n- Rank IC: Spearman correlation between factor cross-section and forward return cross-section\\n- Only dates with >= 8 valid instruments\\n- ICIR = mean(IC)/std(IC)\\n- Hit ratio: fraction of dates where IC has the expected sign\\n- Turnover: mean absolute change in cross-sectional rank (or normalized rank change)\\n- Coverage: fraction of asset-days with valid factor values\\n- Decay: IC at horizons 1, 2, 3, 5, 10, 20\\n\\nAdmission gates: |IC| >= 0.0070 AND |ICIR| >= 0.0840 (on daily IC series, presumably at the admission horizon — the existing factors use horizon 10 as \"admission_horizon\").\\n\\nLet me also compute max_abs_library_correlation: correlation of my factor\\'s daily signal with existing factors\\' signals. Existing library factors need to be re-computed from their JSON definitions:\\n- mom_10d_skip5: close.shift(5)/close.shift(15)-1\\n- mom_120d_skip5: close.shift(5)/close.shift(125)-1 (check file)\\n- vix_beta_cond_60x20: check file\\n- vol_of_vol20x60: check file\\n\\nLet me read the remaining factor files to know their exact expressions.', type='summary_text')], type='reasoning', content=None, encrypted_content=None, status=None)",
